// OmniFlow batch 221 - Knowledge OCR: scanned PDFs and photos of documents are read by the platform vision AI.
//
// Run from the WEBSITE repo root (the bot root - the folder that contains OmniFlow-Control-Plane/):
//     node kb_ocr_221.mjs
// Needs batch 219 (kb_pdf_word_autorefresh_219.mjs) applied first. Safe to run twice (second run says "already").
// Old copies are kept as *.pre_221.bak.
//
// What it does:
//  * Control Plane: portal_kb_files.py - pages with no selectable text that carry a page-sized image (scans) are
//    offered for AI reading; JPEG page images are sent as they are, Flate gray / RGB / indexed images become PNG
//    with the standard library; CCITT fax / JPEG 2000 / CMYK / oversized images use Pillow (lazy, optional).
//    Photos (JPG / PNG / WebP) are read too. Same vision engine, key and AI gate as inbound media (usage feature
//    kb_ocr, shown on the AI usage card). portal_knowledge.py - POST /kb/extract takes ocr:true + pages
//    (a few pages per request). portal_ai_usage.py - "Knowledge document reading (OCR)" label.
//    requirements.txt gets Pillow>=10,<13 (optional - the CP still boots without it).
//  * Website: Knowledge -> Documents & pages: the owner confirms ("uses your AI credits"), pages are read one
//    request at a time with progress + Cancel, the text lands in the same review box, then "Add as draft" as before
//    (also for "Upload new version"). Photos are shrunk in the browser first. Nothing is stored or published by OCR.
//    KB file requests get a longer timeout (OMNIFLOW_KB_FILE_TIMEOUT_MS, default 55000) and the route maxDuration 60.
//  * Tests: tools/cp-testrig/test_kb_ocr.py (93 checks), tools/web-tests/kb_ocr_e2e.py (real Chromium, 15 checks).
//
// Control Plane env (optional, defaults shown): OF_KB_OCR_PAGES_MAX=50  OF_KB_OCR_PAGES_PER_CALL=2
//   OF_KB_OCR_SECONDS=50  OF_KB_OCR_PAGE_SECONDS=40  OF_KB_OCR_MAX_TOKENS=4096  OF_KB_OCR_IMAGE_BYTES_MAX=6000000
//   OF_KB_OCR_RAW_BYTES_MAX=80000000  OF_KB_OCR_MIN_PIXELS=120000  OF_KB_OCR_TEXT_MIN_CHARS=20  OF_KB_OCR_MAX_SIDE=2400
// Vision must be on (Admin -> Integrations -> Image understanding, or OF_VISION_MODE / an AI key).
// After running: CP  git add OmniFlow-Control-Plane... commit, push (Vercel installs Pillow);
//                website  git add -A, commit, push. No other step.
